    "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
    "senderName": "NWS Tiyan GU",
    "headline": "Rip Current Statement issued November 24 at 3:54PM ChST until November 26 at 3:00PM ChST by NWS Tiyan GU",
    "description": "* WHAT...Dangerous rip currents.\n\n* WHERE...East facing reefs of the Marianas.\n\n* WHEN...Through Thursday afternoon.\n\n* IMPACTS...Rip currents can sweep even the best swimmers away from\nshore into deeper water.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...A trade-wind swell will continue to produce\nelevated surf with a high risk of rip currents along east-facing\nreefs at least through Thursday afternoon. Another trade-wind surge\nis possible later this week, potentially continuining the threat of\nrip currents beyond Thursday.",
    "instruction": "Rip currents will be life threatening. If caught in a rip current,\nrelax and float. Don't swim against the current. If able, swim in a\ndirection following the shoreline. If unable to escape, face the shore\nand call or wave for help.",
